# Copy to config.env and edit. config.env is git-ignored: keep anything personal there.

# Where downloads, the extracted source, build products and logs live.
# Needs roughly 1.5 TB free for a full build (about 150 GB if per-module setup files are pruned).
RH_WORKDIR="$REPO_ROOT/work"

# The proof is distributed as 14 parts of one gzip tarball. It is not redistributed here.
RH_PART_URL_PREFIX="https://alpo.ge/lean.tar.gz.part"
RH_PART_COUNT=14
# SHA-256 of the reassembled tarball that this repository's records refer to.
RH_TARBALL_SHA256="9631b4f020199e580ba86178cb56c6e9b09f690c2369a80dc4334aa93f49c7fc"

# Parallel compiler processes. Empty = choose automatically from cores and memory.
RH_JOBS=""

# ---- Google Cloud (only needed for cloud/gcp) ----
GCP_PROJECT=""                 # your project ID
GCP_BUCKET=""                  # a private bucket name of your choosing
GCP_REGION="us-central1"
# Tried in order. Span more than one region: on 2026-11-20 none of the four us-central1 zones had
# capacity for this machine type and the recorded pilot ran in us-east1-b. Quotas are per region.
GCP_ZONES="us-central1-a us-central1-b us-central1-c us-central1-f us-east1-b us-east1-c us-east1-d"
GCP_MACHINE_TYPE="n4d-highmem-32"
GCP_SPEND_CAP_USD=40           # hard cap enforced by the launcher's ledger
# The kernel replay of a full cloud run is leanchecker on every module (criterion C3). Set this to "rhv-replay"
# to have every module replayed a second time by the program in scripts/verify/replay, about six hours more;
# that second replay is not part of the criterion (docs/performance-notes.md, section 10).
GCP_SECOND_REPLAY=""

# ---- Spot runs (launch full-spot | full-spot-rehearsal). All optional; the defaults are shown. ----
# A Spot run is a chain of fresh Spot VMs ("attempts"). Google deletes each one, with its disks, at the attempt's
# own maximum run time or when it takes the machine back; the guest's checkpoints in the bucket carry the work
# from one attempt to the next. Each attempt is sized so that recorded spend can never pass GCP_SPEND_CAP_USD.
# `watch` exits 0 when the run is over and 3 when it has paused (nothing running; `watch` again continues it); a
# full-spot-rehearsal that finished without doing one of its cuts as configured exits 4 (see RUNTAG/cuts.txt).
# When the guest pauses an attempt it says what kind of pause: deadline (the attempt ran out of time) and retry
# (trouble a fresh machine may not have) start the next attempt; stop (another attempt would end the same way)
# pauses the run with the guest's message; parts-limit (below) keeps later attempts in the bucket's region.
# Only one Spot command (launch, watch, teardown, abandon) runs at a time: each holds a lock the kernel keeps on the
# file pilot_state.env.lock in the work folder, which must be on a filesystem with file locks; it ends with the command.
#GCP_SPOT_RATE_USD_PER_HOUR=1.20     # ledger and cap rate for one Spot attempt: machine, disks and address, rounded up
#GCP_SPOT_GIVEUP_HOURS=120           # no attempt starts later than this many hours after the first launch
#GCP_SPOT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=24            # the run pauses once this many attempts have been started
#GCP_SPOT_MIN_ATTEMPT_SECONDS=5400   # an attempt shorter than this is not started (default 2400 for the rehearsal; at least 1500)
#GCP_SPOT_RESERVE_USD=1.00           # kept back from the cap for the bucket storage of the checkpoints, which the ledger does not count
#GCP_SPOT_CKPT_EVERY=600             # seconds between checkpoint archives during the build (default 120 for the rehearsal)
#GCP_SPOT_CONFIRM_EVERY=1200         # seconds between the guest's re-checks of the sealed files, after which replay results are saved (default 45 for the rehearsal; at least 30)
#GCP_XREGION_USD_PER_GIB=0.02        # price of moving data between the bucket's region (read from the bucket itself; it must be one region) and a VM in another region
#                                    #   an attempt outside that region is charged for the parts it restores and adds plus gs://BUCKET/inputs/, which every
#                                    #   attempt downloads (measured at launch); its worst case, GCP_SPOT_PARTS_MAX_GIB plus the inputs, is kept free under the cap
#GCP_SPOT_PARTS_MAX_GIB=60           # bound on all checkpoint archives together: an attempt outside the bucket's region stops saving before they pass it, and none starts there once they pass 90 % of it
#                                    #   once an attempt has stopped at this bound, attempts start only in zones of the bucket's region; if GCP_ZONES has none
#                                    #   the run pauses: add zones of that region to GCP_ZONES, or raise this bound, then run watch. Raising the cap does not help
#GCP_RESULTS_MIRROR_DIR=""           # a local folder (for example one inside Google Drive for desktop) that receives a copy of the small result files
#GCP_SPOT_REHEARSAL_CUTS="build:simulate seal:delete c3:reset"   # rehearsal only: where watch ends an attempt on purpose (build, seal, c2, c3, end) and how (simulate: Google's forced reclaim; delete; reset: a hard reset with no notice)
